Generic calls use ordinary syntax. Immediate evidence selects generic types.
An existing numeric origin can also stay linked through a generic signature
until an exact receiving use resolves it within the same body.

### Inference from an argument

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    identity type A |value A| -> A:
        return value
    ;

    value = identity(42)
]

With no other exact numeric constraint in the body, the whole-number origin
defaults to `I32`, so `A` resolves to `I32`.

### Inference from the result type

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    empty type A || -> {A}:
        return {}
    ;

    items {I32} = empty()
]

The immediate receiving type says the result is `{I32}`, so `A` becomes `I32`.
